Diagnostic kernel module that reproduces the drm-kmod fbdev console damage
overrun: a full-width console rectangle drawn a few scanlines below the bottom
edge of the screen, which the fbdev shadow-buffer damage worker
(drm_fbdev_ttm_helper_fb_dirty via drm_fb_helper_damage_work) then reads past
the end of, panicking a kernel whose drm-kmod lacks the clamp in
drm_fb_helper_damage_area() and cfb_fillrect().

It refuses to do anything unless the active console is the drmfb driver, and it
only fires when debug.fbdamage_repro.go is set to 1, so merely installing or
loading it is harmless.  With the fix in place it clips and survives; without
it, it panics on purpose -- do not run it on a machine you cannot lose.
